# Design Principles — ${PROJECT_NAME} (Frontend React flavor)

> Stability: **stable**. Designed for **power-user admin consoles**.

## 1. Professional density

- Layout targets **desktop 1366×768+**; optimal at 1920×1080.
- Compact tables, row height < 48px, sticky header, persistent filters.
- Avoid huge modals: prefer **side panels** or **detail drawers** that preserve list context.
- Long forms split into **steppers** or navigable sections.

## 2. Coherence and predictability

- Same patterns across all domains: same position of filters, pagination, bulk actions.
- Consistent verbs: "Approve" / "Reject" / "Suspend" / "Reactivate" / "Archive" / "Delete permanently".
- One component variant per purpose (one primary button — not three).

## 3. Perceived safety

- Destructive actions always **double confirmation**: dialog + typing the resource name.
- Mandatory `reason` for: override, hard delete, classification reversal, impersonate.
- Confirmations show "What will happen" (e.g., "234 media will be deleted, 12 classifications left without target").
- Destructive confirmations **not** dismissable accidentally (no close on outside click).

## 4. Long-running operations as first-class citizens

- Every long action → `Job` with dedicated UI.
- Non-blocking toast + "Open job" button.
- Jobs page always reachable from topbar (badge with running count).

## 5. Feedback

- Success: green toast right, auto-dismiss 4s.
- Error: red toast, manual dismiss, copyable `correlationId`.
- In-progress: skeleton; never full-page spinner if cached data exists.
- Empty states: minimal illustration + explanation + doc/action link.

## 6. Persistent filters and Saved Views

- List filters live in the **URL** (`?filter=...&sort=...`).
- Saved Views: saveable, shareable, "pinnable" on dashboard.
- System defaults (read-only) for common cases (e.g., "Devices to approve", "Media in moderation").

## 7. Bulk actions

- Multi-selection with `Shift+click` and `Ctrl+A`.
- Action bar appears above list when ≥ 1 selected.
- Counter + applicable buttons (recomputed by permissions).

## 8. Accessibility

- WCAG 2.1 AA minimum (see NFR).
- Focus always visible, logical order.
- `aria-live` for toasts and job progress.
- Skip-link "Go to main content".
- AAA contrast for body text in dark mode.

## 9. Internationalization

- All strings from dictionary (`${PROJECT_DEFAULT_LOCALE}`/`${PROJECT_FALLBACK_LOCALE}`).
- Date/number formats via `Intl` with admin's locale.
- Correct pluralization (`{count, plural, one {# item} other {# items}}`).

## 10. Dark mode

- Available from day-1, toggle in topbar, saved on profile.
- Neutral palette; accent colors for states (success/warning/error/info).
- Avoid separate assets for dark vs light when possible.

## 11. Standard design-system components

Minimum list (based on shadcn/ui + Radix):

- Button, IconButton, Toggle
- Input, Textarea, Select, Combobox, MultiSelect, DatePicker, RangePicker, Map(picker)
- Table (TanStack), DataGrid wrapper
- Dialog, AlertDialog (destructive), Sheet/Drawer (detail panel)
- Tabs, Accordion, Collapsible
- Badge (status), Pill (filter), Tag
- Toast (sonner-like)
- Skeleton, Spinner (local, not global)
- EmptyState, ErrorState
- StatCard (overview)
- Timeline (audit, job log)
- DiffViewer (config/policy diff)
- JsonEditor (schema-aware)

## 12. User error diagnostics

- Error toast includes `correlationId` (copyable).
- Page `/admin/diagnostics` shows: build version, language, browser locale, last 20 client errors (in memory), anonymized `${ME_ENDPOINT}` info.

## 13. Perceived performance

- Optimistic update only for reversible toggles and tags.
- Prefetch on hover of detail links.
- Route-level code splitting; lazy import for non-landing pages.
- Virtualization for lists > 200 rows.

## 14. What we don't do (motivated constraints)

- We do not introduce competing UI frameworks (Material, Ant) alongside shadcn/ui.
- We do not invent layouts: pages reuse the same templates (list, detail, form, dashboard).
- We do not render unsanitized HTML.
- We do not block the UI on long operations: jobs always.
